The corpus is a single spine of 79 version-pinned systems in two strata — 43
approval substrates and 36 deployed applications — under one threat model and one
selection protocol. Outcomes are mutually exclusive: 54 exposed, 3 conditional,
1 transitive, 19 resistant, 2 non-applicable. Each system carries exactly one
pinned version; the three earlier working corpora are folded in and their
version/verdict conflicts resolved (see RECONCILIATION.md).
